\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. SAVIOUR, and call it be
\par That Thou shouldst dwell with me?
\par From Thy high and lofty throne,
\par Throne of everlasting bliss,
\par Will Thy Majesty stoop down
\par To so mean a house as this?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I am not worthy, Lord,
\par So foul, so self-abhorred,
\par Thee, my God, to entertain
\par In this poor polluted heart:
\par I a frail and sinful man;
\par All my nature cries cries: Depart!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Yet come, Thou heavenly Guest,
\par And purify my breast;
\par Come, Thou great and glorious King,
\par While before Thy Cross I bow;
\par With Thyself salvation bring,
\par Cleanse the house by entering now.
\par                              Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

